alias ExitStatus = std::process::ExitStatus;
alias Inputs = std::process::Inputs;

public fn run(inputs: Inputs) -> status: ExitStatus pure waits doc "The font_face_oracle entry, invoked as `font_face_oracle FONT` with FONT naming a font file relative to the working directory. It loads FONT with load_face and prints, one item per line: `metrics UPEM GLYPHS HHEA_ASC HHEA_DESC HHEA_GAP TYPO_ASC TYPO_DESC TYPO_GAP USE_TYPO WIN_ASC WIN_DESC`, the fields face_metrics returns in declared order; `cmap SCALAR GLYPH` for every Unicode scalar value from 0 to 10FFFF, ascending, whose glyph nominal_glyph returns is not 0; `advance GLYPH ADVANCE` from glyph_advance for every glyph below the metrics' glyph count, ascending; `class GLYPH CLASS` from glyph_class for every such glyph, CLASS 0 to 4 for Unclassified, Base, Ligature, Mark and Component; and `end`. Numbers are decimal, a negative one after a minus sign, except SCALAR, which is lowercase hexadecimal without leading zeros; USE_TYPO is 1 for True and 0 for False. When load_face refuses the font it prints the one line `refused Invalid`, `refused Unsupported` or `refused TooLarge` instead. A font longer than the 268435456 bytes load_face accepts is not passed to it and prints the one line `driver: font too large` instead, and so does a font that read_argument_file refuses as FileTooLarge, past its 2^30-byte limit. It exits with 0 after printing, and with 2, with a message on standard error, when the invocation does not have exactly one argument, FONT cannot be read, or standard output refuses a write.";
